From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: reserve a tag protocol for the BCM5331x VLAN tagger

The Broadcom BCM53314 (StrataXGS) has no CPU header on its Ethernet
ports: the port of a frame exchanged with the host is told by an
802.1Q tag, one VLAN per front port. The tag_8021q encoding codes the
port on 4 bits and does not fit its 19 front ports, so the board uses
a tagger of its own, built out of tree. Give it a protocol number,
outside of the range used upstream.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/include/net/dsa.h
+++ b/include/net/dsa.h
@@ -57,6 +57,8 @@
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_BRCM_LEGACY_FCS_VALUE	29
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_VALUE		30
 #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q_VALUE	31
+/* Local value, kept clear of the upstream range */
+#define DSA_TAG_PROTO_BCM5331X_8021Q_VALUE	64
 
 enum dsa_tag_protocol {
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_NONE		= DSA_TAG_PROTO_NONE_VALUE,
@@ -91,6 +93,7 @@
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_VSC73XX_8021Q	= DSA_TAG_PROTO_VSC73XX_8021Q_VALUE,
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862		= DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_VALUE,
 	DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q	= DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q_VALUE,
+	DSA_TAG_PROTO_BCM5331X_8021Q	= DSA_TAG_PROTO_BCM5331X_8021Q_VALUE,
 };
 
 struct dsa_switch;
